  "review": [
    {
      "section": "time.clock",
      "confidence": "low",
      "note": "Nguni-style ordinal hours: 'lihora lesitsatfu' (the third hour) = 3 o'clock, 'lihora lekucala' = 1 o'clock, 'lihora lelishumi nakubili' = 12. Minutes: 'lihora {h} nemizuzu lelishumi' (class-4 concords: lemihlanu, lelishumi, lelishumi nesihlanu, lemashumi lamabili ...); half 'nenhafu' (as the file's duration data). Doubts: siSwati class-4/class-6 concord forms for the minute numerals are modelled on isiZulu and may be off; speakers often say 'hafu pasi' colloquially. Hours 9 in the old data ('sifisagcina') replaced with 'lemfica'. Needs native review."
    }
  ]
